After the function returns, `_setCollapsed` updates `_collapsedBlockIds` and then calls `_recompute`, which seems fine. But for programmatic selection, if `controller.setSelection` is hidden and triggers the outline to notify, `_recompute` may not change anything if the collapsed state is active. Then, if `expandToRevealSelection` modifies `_collapsedBlockIds`, it will again call `_recompute` to notify. I wonder if there's no need to call `setState` since the widget listens to both the controller and the outline. That makes things more efficient!
